WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.111
Which came first:

00:00:01.121 --> 00:00:03.243
toilet paper, or the printing press?

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:04.514
Comment your answer.

00:00:04.524 --> 00:00:07.952
This Gutenberg Bible was printed in Mainz

00:00:07.962 --> 00:00:09.094
around 1455.

00:00:09.194 --> 00:00:11.439
But in China, around 589, a scholar

00:00:11.449 --> 00:00:13.944
named Yan Zhitui wrote that he would

00:00:13.954 --> 00:00:16.699
never use pages quoting the classics on

00:00:16.709 --> 00:00:17.611
the toilet.

00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:21.180
Toilet paper wins, by about 850 years.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:24.888
By the 1300s, China's imperial court got

00:00:24.898 --> 00:00:27.018
720,000 sheets a year.
